  "rule": "Rule by vtable slot. The shape classes are ShapeBase (phys_fn_001273) and the six classes whose constructors call it; the tables below are the eight vtables those seven constructors store, each with the store that establishes it. A slot is a collision slot when the collision pipeline dispatches through it: a virtual call through that slot on a receiver of the table's class, from a row the pipeline reaches -- the 39 matrix slots phys_fn_002338 fills, the rows they call and the callbacks they pass -- or from the Prunable owner adapter the pipeline reaches through phys_fn_004886. Every other slot is an object-model slot. The slot's name decides nothing; the sites in slot_evidence do. A slot target takes the phase of its slot, collision 3 and object model 5, and a row several slots name must get one phase from all of them or be listed as an exception. A row that stores a shape table -- a constructor or a destructor -- is object model. The two Prunable owner adapters take the phase of the one slot their body calls. A helper, a row whose every direct caller is a ruled row and which has no translation unit, export pin or table of its own, takes the one phase its callers are ruled to. A body the linker folded and shared outside the shape classes is shared runtime, Phase 2; a body another translation unit owns is left to it. Every ruled row, and every continuation row of one, records phase_provenance slot_ruling, and validate_inventory.py recomputes the phase from this file. A direct call from the collision pipeline into an object-model row does not move it: phys_fn_001874, the [MESH][MESH] vertex callback phys_fn_001876 passes at 0x00046d15, builds two temporary SphereShapes through phys_fn_001349, phys_fn_001357 and phys_fn_001351 as a client of the object model.",
